# NebulaOS mutable-runtime mission, Memory Resilience Gate (2026-07-26):
# real bug found live on the actual device - `swapon -p 100 /dev/zram0`
# failed outright ("swapon: invalid option -- 'p'"), and the documented
# BusyBox workaround (an /etc/fstab entry with a "pri=" mount option,
# activated via `swapon -a`) DID bring the swap area up but silently
# ignored the requested priority (confirmed live: /proc/swaps showed
# priority -2, not the requested 100) - because
# CONFIG_FEATURE_SWAPON_PRI was not enabled in this project's BusyBox
# build at all (confirmed directly against
# vendor/buildroot-x2000/package/busybox/busybox.config, not guessed).
# Without this, there is no way to make the NebulaOS disk swap file
# genuinely lower-priority than zram, which this whole memory-resilience
# design depends on.
CONFIG_FEATURE_SWAPON_PRI=y
